cff-version: 1.2.0
title: quranbench
message: >-
  If you use this corpus, this software, or a query reproduced from this site in
  academic work, please cite it. Cite the corpus version you actually used — the
  version is printed on every page and returned by every API response, and each
  version is independently checksummed.
type: software
authors:
  # The maintainer's public name is not yet decided (see apps/web/src/lib/site.ts).
  # Nothing in this project asserts a name that has not been chosen, so the project
  # itself is named as the author for now. Replace this entry with the person or
  # organisation when that decision is made, and add an ORCID.
  - name: quranbench
    website: 'https://quranbench.com'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/halostudios99-bit/quranbench'
url: 'https://quranbench.com'
abstract: >-
  An open Quran research workbench. Every Arabic word is a permanent, addressable
  research object with its own page: forms, position, root and morphology, every
  other occurrence of the same form, and how translators rendered the surrounding
  verse. Search runs over the text by its own words — form, root, lemma, pattern,
  proximity — and every result carries the corpus version and the query that
  produced it, so any figure on the site can be reproduced by a third party.
keywords:
  - Quran
  - Arabic
  - corpus linguistics
  - digital humanities
  - morphology
  - reproducible research
  - open data
license: MIT
license-url: 'https://github.com/halostudios99-bit/quranbench/blob/main/LICENSE'
version: 0.8.0
date-released: '2026-07-26'
references:
  - type: data
    title: Tanzil Quran Text (Uthmani)
    notes: >-
      The Arabic source text. CC BY 3.0. Never modified; normalised and segmented
      forms are stored as separate labelled fields.
    url: 'https://tanzil.net/'
  - type: data
    title: Quranic Arabic Corpus (Leeds)
    notes: >-
      Morphological annotation, glosses and transliteration. GPL-2.0-or-later.
      tokens.jsonl embeds this and is therefore GPL as a whole — see LICENSING.md.
    url: 'https://corpus.quran.com/'
  - type: data
    title: "Lane's Arabic-English Lexicon (Perseus/Tufts)"
    notes: 'CC BY-SA 3.0. Covers 1,564 of 1,651 roots (94.7%).'
